  "summary": "The exact source passed independent Chrome development with a separately installed retained Core. Native AMD64 Web upgraded from 1.8.2 to 1.9.1 and rolled back to 1.8.2. Authenticated Inbox, the original session and durable records survived both transitions. Core, PostgreSQL, Worker, Realtime and all 120 migration entries were retained. The native v4 smoke, registry and collector steps verified mandatory Core and its readiness with Web offline, registry round-trip and signed Operations Collector delivery.",
  "limitations": "These source and disposable runtime checks used synthetic accounts and data. Live ingress, installed diagnostic collection, provider operations and product acceptance remain separate. The first full-image run held at the browser receipt assertion for the new diagnostics field, before artifact custody. Merge requires the corrected browser assertion and a successful complete qualification run. Exact-main CI, CodeQL and image qualification remain publication requirements.",
